KG42.register("clusters-87e24bc72d59d2491af89772",{"id":"36-dsm_mechanism_design::v142-d-K001","paper":"36-dsm_mechanism_design","label":"VCG demand reporting, welfare allocation, and Clarke-tax settlement","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K001","label":"VCG demand reporting, welfare allocation, and Clarke-tax settlement","market_meaning":"Users submit demand types, the energy provider selects the welfare-optimal allocation based on the reported information, and in the branch where the Clarke tax is selected it calculates individual payments. Truthfulness, efficiency, consumer non-negative payments, and the payment upper bound each retain their original conditions; the reporting feasible region and some theorem conditions have not yet been closed.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["DEM"],"process_stages":["bidding","clearing","settlement"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"R001 and R002 contain the general VCG payment construction, and the specific settlement in R003 adopts the Clarke-tax choice. True demand and reported demand, and the complete system and the user-excluded scenario, are retained separately; non-negative transfers are limited to the consumer model, and the payment upper bound is interpreted according to allocation under true information and the original theorem conditions.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"Reported information determines allocation, the allocations of the complete system and the user-excluded system determine payments, and the payment construction in turn supports truthfulness and, under its conditions, efficiency, forming an identifiable closed loop of information, decisions, and obligations. The boundary is based on these interfaces under the same mechanism; gaps remain in the mathematical applicability conditions.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R001","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"This provides the demand-reporting obligation, private types, and the truthfulness conditions under general VCG payments."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"This provides the decision from reported information to welfare allocation and the efficiency result under truthful reporting."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R003","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"This provides the specific Clarke-tax settlement and its conditional payment properties."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-N01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X001","v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-T001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::I_hat","v141-c-R002::theta::I_true","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e013","v141-b-g02-e014","v141-b-g02-e017"],"rationale":"The true and reported types of an individual user respectively compose the information profile of all users, and the reported profile enters the allocation rule. This interface retains the individual and aggregate levels and does not identify the two types of objects as the same quantity."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-N02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::x_nk","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-xnk","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e017","v141-b-g02-e021","v141-b-g02-e022"],"rationale":"The allocation of the complete system enters the payment calculation; the allocation after excluding a user is solved separately according to the same allocation rule. The evaluations of the complete system and the counterfactual scenario remain distinct."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-N03","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e018","v141-b-g02-e021","v141-b-g02-e022"],"rationale":"The arbitrary other-agent information function in the general payment is specified in the Clarke-tax branch as the welfare value after excluding the user. The two constraints are a general construction and a conditional specific choice, and they are not merged as duplicate expressions."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-N04","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002","v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-Ihat-minus-n"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e018","v141-b-g02-e019","v141-b-g02-e021","v141-b-g02-e022"],"rationale":"The Clarke-tax choice uses only other agents' reported information and belongs to a specific branch of the general VCG payment construction; it therefore connects with the truthfulness conclusion retained in R001. The reporting-feasibility issue remains in the gaps."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-N05","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e019","v141-b-g02-e020"],"rationale":"The source links each user's truthful-reporting dominant strategy with the efficiency result when all users report truthfully. The assembly retains the condition that all users report truthfully and does not directly equate the existence of a dominant strategy with actual truthful reporting."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-O01","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R002::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R003::V::bidding.demand"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R001::V::bidding.demand","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e013","v141-b-g02-e017","v141-b-g03-e01-vcg-declaration"],"rationale":"All three places refer to the user demand-reporting activity of the same VCG mechanism; a node in the reporting chain is selected as the display representative, and all original references are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-O02","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::settlement.payment","v141-c-R002::V::settlement.payment","v141-c-R003::V::settlement.payment"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R003::V::settlement.payment","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e018","v141-b-g02-e022"],"rationale":"The three places use the same payment-function node. The display representative does not eliminate the conditional difference between the general VCG construction and the specific Clarke-tax choice."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-O03","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::V::clearing.social_welfare","v141-c-R003::V::clearing.social_welfare"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R002::V::clearing.social_welfare","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e017","v141-b-g02-e021","v141-b-g02-e022"],"rationale":"Both places are the welfare-allocation function of this VCG mechanism; the complete-system and user-excluded scenarios are still interpreted separately according to the respective constraints."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-O04","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::I_hat","v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-Ihat"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e014","v141-b-g02-e017","v141-b-g02-e022"],"rationale":"Both are the reported demand profile of all users, serving respectively as inputs to allocation and settlement; the local parameter objects are retained and are not merged with individual reports or the user-excluded profile."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-O05","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::I_true","v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-I"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e014","v141-b-g02-e020","v141-b-g02-e024"],"rationale":"Both refer to the true demand profile of all users, used respectively for the efficiency condition and for evaluating the payment upper bound; their respective local roles are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K001-O06","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::x_nk","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-xnk"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e017","v141-b-g02-e021","v141-b-g02-e022"],"rationale":"Under the same user, time period and complete declaration profile, the two refer to the same consumption component generated by the allocation rule. The local feasible-region formulation and the different evaluations for true information, declared information, excluded users, and the like remain distinguished."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K001-G01","category":"math_incomplete","description":"R001-C001 universally quantifies over alternative declarations, but frozen C does not restrict the declarable types or the executability of the allocation under the false-reporting feasible set; the consumption object of R002 uses the true feasible region, whereas the allocation rule uses the declared feasible region. The existing interface cannot prove that the two regions coincide.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001","v141-c-R002::x::x_nk","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C005","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-x-xnk"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e013","v141-b-g02-e017","v141-b-g02-e019","v141-b-g02-e022"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check how the source treats permitted declarations, physical executability, and the true and declared feasible regions; upstream is to supply the missing conditions; retain the current frozen expression and local objects."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K001-G02","category":"math_incomplete","description":"Properties 1-4 and Assumptions 1-3 cited by the payment property are not expanded in the frozen constraints; the scope of application between the zero-point condition of cost definition (8) and the fixed term permitted by (9) still needs clarification, and it cannot automatically be concluded that all permitted parameters simultaneously satisfy Assumption 3.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C004","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C003","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E14","v141-b-g01-E17","v141-b-g01-E18","v141-b-g02-e023","v141-b-g02-e024"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the theorem premises, cost normalization and fixed-term treatment, supply the references to conditions of the same mechanism, and have their mathematical compatibility checked manually."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K001-G03","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The optimality condition (27) cited by the payment upper bound does not list the branch in which the maximum-power constraint is binding, and frozen C also does not provide the complete price and optimality conditions. This cluster retains the original upper-bound assertion, but its proof interface has not yet been closed.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::M_nk","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C005","v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-theta-lambda-star","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g02-e024","v141-b-g03-e12-eq27"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the complete optimality conditions and upper-bound proof when the maximum-power and total-energy constraints are binding; maintain the benchmark range of the optimal clearing price and do not identify it with arbitrary prices from other mechanisms."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K001-G04","category":"ontology_extension","description":"The generic declaration and payment nodes do not yet specifically express the VCG transfer structure or the dominant-strategy property of truthful declaration; the related node proposals have still not been approved.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001","v141-c-R003::V::settlement.payment","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E29","v141-b-g02-e018","v141-b-g02-e022","v141-b-g03-e04-truthfulness-definition"],"proposal_ids":["proposal:v141-b-g01-P03","proposal:v141-b-g03-truthful-dominant-strategy"],"required_work":"Have the node-extension proposals and their relations to existing nodes checked manually; this round continues to reference only frozen objects."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K001-G05","category":"unverified_source","description":"The B evidence cited by this cluster all remains unverified and has only experimental candidate-support status; it has not undergone B source audit, C2 independent review, or Agent E examination.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e013","v141-b-g02-e014","v141-b-g02-e017","v141-b-g02-e018","v141-b-g02-e019","v141-b-g02-e020","v141-b-g02-e021","v141-b-g02-e022","v141-b-g02-e023","v141-b-g02-e024"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the citations, formula transcriptions, applicable conditions and assembly mappings item by item, and maintain the current source status until the review is actually completed."}]},"rule_refs":["36-dsm_mechanism_design::v141-c-R001","36-dsm_mechanism_design::v141-c-R002","36-dsm_mechanism_design::v141-c-R003"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-20a5cdf8b3b1e9c9","COMP-ebacec241379c91d","KG40-14a3066c15f25075"]});
